The already registered g-like clock relation is $$\boxed{\frac{g}{2}=\frac{\omega_s}{\omega_c}.}$$ Define the corresponding quantum energy scales $$\mathcal E_s=\hbar\omega_s,\qquad
\mathcal E_c=\hbar\omega_c.$$ Then $$\boxed{
\frac{g}{2}=\frac{\omega_s}{\omega_c}=\frac{\mathcal E_s}{\mathcal E_c}.
}$$ Writing $$\omega_a=\omega_s-\omega_c,\qquad
\Delta\mathcal E_a=\hbar\omega_a,$$ we also obtain $$\boxed{
\frac{g}{2}
=1+\frac{\omega_a}{\omega_c}
=1+\frac{\Delta\mathcal E_a}{\mathcal E_c}.
}$$ This translation requires no measured numerical value of $g$. It is an exact change of language from the already registered frequency ratio to the corresponding energy-scale ratio.
